            data: {
              text: "# MLOps Risk Assessment\n\n## Critical Risks\n\n### Technical Risks\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Notes |\n|------|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Model drift/degradation | High | High | Production data diverges from training data over time |\n| Pipeline failures | Medium | High | Automated CI/CD breaks silently |\n| Data quality issues | High | High | Garbage in, garbage out at scale |\n| Version incompatibility | Medium | Medium | Model/data/code versioning misalignment |\n\n### Operational Risks\n- **Monitoring gaps** — Metrics may not capture meaningful model failures\n- **Dependency sprawl** — Complex toolchains create fragile systems\n- **Rollback difficulty** — Reverting deployed models is often harder than software\n\n### Governance & Compliance Risks\n- **Audit trail gaps** — Insufficient logging of model decisions\n- **Regulatory exposure** — GDPR, AI Act, sector-specific rules\n- **Bias propagation** — Automated deployment accelerates harmful outputs at scale\n\n### Organizational Risks\n- **Skill gaps** — Requires hybrid ML + DevOps + data engineering expertise\n- **Ownership ambiguity** — Unclear accountability between data science and engineering teams\n\n---\n\n## Priority Recommendations\n\n1. **Implement automated drift detection** before scaling deployments\n2. **Define clear rollback procedures** for every production model\n3. **Establish governance checkpoints** in CI/CD pipelines, not after\n4. **Document ownership explicitly** for each model in production\n\n---\n\n## Key Observation\n> The greatest compounded risk is **automation without adequate monitoring** — MLOps accelerates both value delivery *and* failure propagation simultaneously.\n\nWould you like deeper analysis on any specific risk category?",
            },
            data_text:
              "                                       MLOps Risk Assessment                                        \n\nCritical Risks                                                                                      \n\nTechnical Risks                                                                                     \n\n                                                                                                    \n Risk                     Likelihood  Impact  Notes                                                 \n ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── \n Model drift/degradation  High        High    Production data diverges from training data over time \n Pipeline failures        Medium      High    Automated CI/CD breaks silently                       \n Data quality issues      High        High    Garbage in, garbage out at scale                      \n Version incompatibility  Medium      Medium  Model/data/code versioning misalignment               \n                                                                                                    \n\nOperational Risks                                                                                   \n\n • Monitoring gaps — Metrics may not capture meaningful model failures                              \n • Dependency sprawl — Complex toolchains create fragile systems                                    \n • Rollback difficulty — Reverting deployed models is often harder than software                    \n\nGovernance & Compliance Risks                                                                       \n\n • Audit trail gaps — Insufficient logging of model decisions                                       \n • Regulatory exposure — GDPR, AI Act, sector-specific rules                                        \n • Bias propagation — Automated deployment accelerates harmful outputs at scale                     \n\nOrganizational Risks                                                                                \n\n • Skill gaps — Requires hybrid ML + DevOps + data engineering expertise                            \n • Ownership ambiguity — Unclear accountability between data science and engineering teams          \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPriority Recommendations                                                                            \n\n 1 Implement automated drift detection before scaling deployments                                   \n 2 Define clear rollback procedures for every production model                                      \n 3 Establish governance checkpoints in CI/CD pipelines, not after                                   \n 4 Document ownership explicitly for each model in production                                       \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKey Observation                                                                                     \n\n▌ The greatest compounded risk is automation without adequate monitoring — MLOps accelerates both \n▌ value delivery and failure propagation simultaneously.                                          \n\nWould you like deeper analysis on any specific risk category?                                       \n",
            data_html:
              "# MLOps Risk Assessment\n\n## Critical Risks\n\n### Technical Risks\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Notes |\n|------|-----------|--------|-------|\n| Model drift/degradation | High | High | Production data diverges from training data over time |\n| Pipeline failures | Medium | High | Automated CI/CD breaks silently |\n| Data quality issues | High | High | Garbage in, garbage out at scale |\n| Version incompatibility | Medium | Medium | Model/data/code versioning misalignment |\n\n### Operational Risks\n- **Monitoring gaps** — Metrics may not capture meaningful model failures\n- **Dependency sprawl** — Complex toolchains create fragile systems\n- **Rollback difficulty** — Reverting deployed models is often harder than software\n\n### Governance &amp; Compliance Risks\n- **Audit trail gaps** — Insufficient logging of model decisions\n- **Regulatory exposure** — GDPR, AI Act, sector-specific rules\n- **Bias propagation** — Automated deployment accelerates harmful outputs at scale\n\n### Organizational Risks\n- **Skill gaps** — Requires hybrid ML + DevOps + data engineering expertise\n- **Ownership ambiguity** — Unclear accountability between data science and engineering teams\n\n---\n\n## Priority Recommendations\n\n1. **Implement automated drift detection** before scaling deployments\n2. **Define clear rollback procedures** for every production model\n3. **Establish governance checkpoints** in CI/CD pipelines, not after\n4. **Document ownership explicitly** for each model in production\n\n---\n\n## Key Observation\n&gt; The greatest compounded risk is **automation without adequate monitoring** — MLOps accelerates both value delivery *and* failure propagation simultaneously.\n\nWould you like deeper analysis on any specific risk category?",
