              "                                     Technical Analysis: MLOps                                      \n\nStructural Decomposition                                                                            \n\nCore Definition                                                                                     \n\nMLOps = Practices + Tools + Organizational Structures applied to ML model lifecycle management      \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nComponent Analysis                                                                                  \n\n                                                                       \n Component          Function                               Criticality \n ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── \n Data Versioning    Reproducibility & lineage tracking     High        \n Model Registry     Centralized model artifact management  High        \n Automated Testing  Quality assurance gates                High        \n CI/CD              Deployment pipeline automation         High        \n Monitoring         Production performance tracking        Critical    \n Governance         Compliance & accountability            High        \n                                                                       \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDependency Mapping                                                                                  \n\n                                                                                                    \n Data Versioning ──────────────┐                                                                    \n                               ▼                                                                    \n Automated Testing ──→ Model Registry ──→ CI/CD ──→ Production                                      \n                               │                        │                                           \n Governance ───────────────────┘         Monitoring ◄──┘                                            \n                                                                                                    \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCritical Observations                                                                               \n\nStrengths of Framework                                                                              \n\n • Holistic scope — addresses people, process, and technology                                       \n • Lifecycle coverage — spans development through maintenance                                       \n\nIdentified Gaps                                                                                     \n\n • No mention of feature stores — significant omission for data management                          \n • Feedback loops — monitoring outputs should explicitly feed back into retraining                  \n • Scalability mechanisms — no reference to infrastructure orchestration                            \n • Security — absent from governance definition                                                     \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nRisk Assessment                                                                                     \n\n                                                                                                    \n HIGH RISK AREAS:                                                                                   \n ├── Model drift (requires robust monitoring)                                                       \n ├── Data quality degradation (versioning alone insufficient)                                       \n └── Governance ambiguity (undefined accountability structures)                                     \n                                                                                                    \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nRecommendations                                                                                     \n\n 1 Extend governance to explicitly include model explainability and bias detection                  \n 2 Define feedback loops between monitoring and retraining pipelines                                \n 3 Add feature store as a seventh core component                                                    \n 4 Specify testing types — unit, integration, shadow deployment, A/B testing                        \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nMaturity Assessment                                                                                 \n\nThe definition represents a Level 2-3 MLOps maturity framework — structured but lacking explicit    \nautomation of retraining and advanced observability.                                                \n",
            data_html:
              "# Technical Analysis: MLOps\n\n## Structural Decomposition\n\n### Core Definition\nMLOps = **Practices** + **Tools** + **Organizational Structures** applied to ML model lifecycle management\n\n---\n\n## Component Analysis\n\n| Component | Function | Criticality |\n|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| Data Versioning | Reproducibility &amp; lineage tracking | High |\n| Model Registry | Centralized model artifact management | High |\n| Automated Testing | Quality assurance gates | High |\n| CI/CD | Deployment pipeline automation | High |\n| Monitoring | Production performance tracking | Critical |\n| Governance | Compliance &amp; accountability | High |\n\n---\n\n## Dependency Mapping\n\n```\nData Versioning ──────────────┐\n                              ▼\nAutomated Testing ──→ Model Registry ──→ CI/CD ──→ Production\n                              │                        │\nGovernance ───────────────────┘         Monitoring ◄──┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Critical Observations\n\n### Strengths of Framework\n- **Holistic scope** — addresses people, process, and technology\n- **Lifecycle coverage** — spans development through maintenance\n\n### Identified Gaps\n- **No mention of feature stores** — significant omission for data management\n- **Feedback loops** — monitoring outputs should explicitly feed back into retraining\n- **Scalability mechanisms** — no reference to infrastructure orchestration\n- **Security** — absent from governance definition\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n```\nHIGH RISK AREAS:\n├── Model drift (requires robust monitoring)\n├── Data quality degradation (versioning alone insufficient)\n└── Governance ambiguity (undefined accountability structures)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Extend governance** to explicitly include model explainability and bias detection\n2. **Define feedback loops** between monitoring and retraining pipelines\n3. **Add feature store** as a seventh core component\n4. **Specify testing types** — unit, integration, shadow deployment, A/B testing\n\n---\n\n## Maturity Assessment\n\nThe definition represents a **Level 2-3 MLOps maturity** framework — structured but lacking explicit automation of retraining and advanced observability.",
